     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The current FDA label for sertraline (Zoloft) sets a maximum of 200 mg/day for adults, across all its indications. 1000 mg is five times that limit, so the label doesn't support it. I'd be knowingly entering a potentially dangerous overdose-level order, so I'm not going to do that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Tell me the dose, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or the prescriber.** If the patient has a clinical situation that needs something unusual, a clinical pharmacist or psychiatry consult can review it and arrange the right order pathway.\n- **Check what's wrong with the dose.** If 1000 mg came from a transcription error or a unit mix-up, I can help you work out the intended dose.\n\nIf this is a real overdose or ingestion, contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) and the treating team. That would need a clinical response, not a medication order."
      }
     ],
